    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15073" root="رحل" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرْتَحَلٌ</span></b>  signifies [The <i>act of removing</i> or <i>departing;</i> i. e.] the <i>contr. of</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَحَلٌّ</span> used in the
sense of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُلُولٌ</span>. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And sometimes it signifies The <i>place in which one alights,</i> or <i>descends
and stops.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  Also The <i>place of the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَحْل</span>
[which may here mean either the <i>saddle</i> or the
<i>saddling</i>] of a camel. (TA.)

